---
layout: default
title: Questions
permalink: /questions/
sitemap_priority: 0.7
sitemap_changefreq: weekly
description: >-
  Straight answers to the problems architects and engineering leaders
  actually run into: slow microservices, outages, cloud bills, AI-generated
  code, and where to start with an AI strategy.
---

<%
  # Curated order, as with series: `order` in each question's front matter is
  # editorial. The builder has already dropped any question with no live
  # article from a production build, so everything in the collection shows.
  questions = site.collections.questions.resources.sort_by { |q| q.data.order || 999 }
%>

<header class="listing-header">
  <h1>Questions</h1>
  <p class="listing-description">
    The problems readers bring me, not the topics I'd pick. Each page gives a
    short answer first, then the articles that go deeper.
  </p>
</header>

<ol class="series-index">
  <% questions.each do |question| %>
    <%
      key = question.basename_without_ext
      count = site.collections.articles.resources.count { |r| Array(r.data.questions).include?(key) }
    %>
    <li class="series-index-item">
      <a href="<%= relative_url question.relative_url %>" class="series-index-title"><%= question.data.title %></a>
      <p class="series-index-meta"><%= count %> <%= count == 1 ? "article" : "articles" %></p>
      <p class="series-index-description"><%= question.data.description %></p>
      <a href="<%= relative_url question.relative_url %>" class="article-list-readmore">Read the answer &rarr;</a>
    </li>
  <% end %>
</ol>
